        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "The interpolated y-value.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "kind" : "content"
    },
    {
      "content" : [
        {
          "anchor" : "discussion",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Discussion",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "Catmull-Rom splines create smooth C¹-continuous curves that pass through",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "all control points. The curve is defined piecewise between consecutive",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "points, using neighboring points as control points to determine tangents.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "anchor" : "Algorithm",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Algorithm",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "For each segment between points P₁ and P₂, the curve uses four points",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "(P₀, P₁, P₂, P₃) where P₀ and P₃ are the neighboring control points:",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "code" : [
            "P(t) = 0.5 × [(2P₁) +",
            "              (-P₀ + P₂)t +",
            "              (2P₀ - 5P₁ + 4P₂ - P₃)t² +",
            "              (-P₀ + 3P₁ - 3P₂ + P₃)t³]"
          ],
          "syntax" : null,
          "type" : "codeListing"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "where t ∈ [0, 1] is the normalized position within the segment.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "anchor" : "Endpoint-Handling",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Endpoint Handling",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "At the endpoints where we lack neighboring control points, the function",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "extrapolates virtual control points to maintain smoothness:",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "items" : [
            {
              "content" : [
                {
                  "inlineContent" : [
                    {
                      "text" : "Before first segment: reflects the tangent at the first point",
                      "type" : "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type" : "paragraph"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "content" : [
                {
                  "inlineContent" : [
                    {
                      "text" : "After last segment: reflects the tangent at the last point",
                      "type" : "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type" : "paragraph"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "type" : "unorderedList"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "For x values outside the range of defined points, the function clamps",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "to the nearest endpoint value.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "anchor" : "Edge-Cases",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Edge Cases",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "items" : [
            {
              "content" : [
                {
                  "inlineContent" : [
                    {
                      "text" : "Single point: Returns that point’s y-value for all x",
                      "type" : "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type" : "paragraph"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "content" : [
                {
                  "inlineContent" : [
                    {
                      "text" : "Two points: Falls back to linear interpolation",
                      "type" : "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type" : "paragraph"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "type" : "unorderedList"
        }
      ],
      "kind" : "content"
    }
